come, none of your descendants who has a physical defect may approach to offer the food of his God.","verse":17},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Aaron","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Aaron::Aaron::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Aaron"},"text":"No descendant of Aaron the priest who has a defect shall approach to present the food offerings to the LORD. Since he has a defect, he is not to come near to offer the food of his God.","verse":21},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Aaron","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Aaron::Aaron::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Aaron"},"text":"Moses told this to Aaron and his sons and to all the Israelites.","verse":24}],"id":"Aaron","label":"Aaron","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Aaron::Aaron::reviewed_unambiguous_name","scope":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","senseReview":"Reviewed complete original name headword and source subject. Article covers the biblical person(s), named place, or named spiritual figure denoted by this exact spelling; multiple persons under one unchanged source article remain together. Actual proper-name capitalization and whole-name boundaries required. Explicit occurrence-level ambiguity exclusions override this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Aaron","term":"Aaron"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Aaron","sourceTitle":"Aaron"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Then the LORD said to Moses, “Speak to Aaron’s sons, the priests, and tell them that a priest is not to defile himself for a dead person among his people,","verse":1},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"They must be holy to their God and not profane the name of their God. Because they present to the LORD the food offerings, the food of their God, they must be holy.","verse":6},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"You are to regard him as holy, since he presents the food of your God. He shall be holy to you, because I the LORD am holy—I who set you apart.","verse":8},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"He must not leave or desecrate the sanctuary of his God, for the consecration of the anointing oil of his God is on him. I am the LORD.","verse":12},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"so that he does not defile his offspring among his people, for I am the LORD who sanctifies him.”","verse":15},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Then the LORD said to Moses,","verse":16},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"No descendant of Aaron the priest who has a defect shall approach to present the food offerings to the LORD. Since he has a defect, he is not to come near to offer the food of his God.","verse":21},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"but because he has a defect, he must not go near the veil or approach the altar, so as not to desecrate My sanctuaries. For I am the LORD who sanctifies them.’”","verse":23}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Moses","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Moses::Moses::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Moses"},"text":"Then the LORD said to Moses, “Speak to Aaron’s sons, the priests, and tell them that a priest is not to defile himself for a dead person among his people,","verse":1},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Moses","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Moses::Moses::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Moses"},"text":"Then the LORD said to Moses,","verse":16},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Moses","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Moses::Moses::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Moses"},"text":"Moses told this to Aaron and his sons and to all the Israelites.","verse":24}],"id":"Moses","label":"Moses","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Moses::Moses::reviewed_unambiguous_name","scope":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","senseReview":"Reviewed complete original name headword and source subject. Article covers the biblical person(s), named place, or named spiritual figure denoted by this exact spelling; multiple persons under one unchanged source article remain together. Actual proper-name capitalization and whole-name boundaries required. Explicit occurrence-level ambiguity exclusions override this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Moses","term":"Moses"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Moses","sourceTitle":"Moses"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.1-22.33","r":"Lev.21.1-22.33","rawR":"Lev.21.1-22.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.1-22.33","value":"Lev.21.1-22.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:1–22:33"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This section, which covers priestly regulations, is punctuated six times with the phrase ",{"c":["I am the"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt-divine-name","t":"span"},{"c":[" who makes . . . holy"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.15","r":"Lev.21.15","rawR":"Lev.21.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.15","value":"Lev.21.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:15"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.23","r":"Lev.21.23","rawR":"Lev.21.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.23","value":"Lev.21.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.22.9","r":"Lev.22.9","rawR":"Lev.22.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.22.9","value":"Lev.22.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:9"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.22.16","r":"Lev.22.16","rawR":"Lev.22.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.22.16","value":"Lev.22.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"16"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.22.32","r":"Lev.22.32","rawR":"Lev.22.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.22.32","value":"Lev.22.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"32"},"; cp. ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.8","r":"Lev.21.8","rawR":"Lev.21.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.8","value":"Lev.21.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:8"},"). The words reaffirm the necessary connection between the holiness of God and the holiness expected of the priesthood, and by extension, of all Israel (see ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.8.10","r":"Lev.8.10","rawR":"Lev.8.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.8.10","value":"Lev.8.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.11.44-45","r":"Lev.11.44-45","rawR":"Lev.11.44-45","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.11.44-45","value":"Lev.11.44-45"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:44-45"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.19.2","r":"Lev.19.2","rawR":"Lev.19.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.19.2","value":"Lev.19.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:2"},"). Priests are specifically addressed in ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.1-22.16","r":"Lev.21.1-22.16","rawR":"Lev.21.1-22.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.1-22.16","value":"Lev.21.1-22.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:1–22:16"},", while both clergy and laity are included in ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.22.17-33","r":"Lev.22.17-33","rawR":"Lev.22.17-33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.22.17-33","value":"Lev.22.17-33"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:17-33"},"."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Lev.21.1-22.33","refs":[{"book":"LEV","endChapter":22,"endVerse":33,"startChapter":21,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Lev.21.1-22.33","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"LEV","sourceChapterCoverage":[21,22],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"169235906cbc0609d7bd55270f3bf9f4454b5b507e07c6314aa77c4823db91c1","sourceItemName":"Lev.21.1-22.33","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":1497,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"LEV","canonicalOSIS":"Lev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Lev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Lev.21.1-22.33","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Lev.21.1-22.33","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.1-4","r":"Lev.21.1-4","rawR":"Lev.21.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.1-4","value":"Lev.21.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:1-4"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," Touching a ",{"c":["dead body"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," rendered a person unclean for seven days. Because a priest had to be prepared to deal with holy things at all times, he was not allowed to handle a dead body, even of a relative, or else he could be unfit to minister when needed. The only exceptions were his ",{"c":["closest relatives"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," because there might not be anyone else who could bury the bodies."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Lev.21.1-4","refs":[{"book":"LEV","endChapter":21,"endVerse":4,"startChapter":21,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Lev.21.1-4","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"LEV","sourceChapterCoverage":[21],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"9b07f34307cb35f987b47c445a419fff26ebb72f04f2063d3e2a6aaf9a3ec4bd","sourceItemName":"Lev.21.1-4","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":1498,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"LEV","canonicalOSIS":"Lev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Lev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Lev.21.1-4","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Lev.21.1-4","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.5","r":"Lev.21.5","rawR":"Lev.21.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.5","value":"Lev.21.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:5"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["shave . . . trim:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," See study notes on ",{"href":"?item=Lev.10.6_StudyNote_Filament","id":"Lev.10.6_StudyNote_Filament","rawId":"Lev.10.6_StudyNote_Filament","t":"link","v":"10:6"},"; ",{"href":"?item=Lev.19.27_StudyNote_Filament","id":"Lev.19.27_StudyNote_Filament","rawId":"Lev.19.27_StudyNote_Filament","t":"link","v":"19:27"},". • ",{"c":["cut their bodies:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," See ",{"href":"?item=Lev.19.28_StudyNote_Filament","id":"Lev.19.28_StudyNote_Filament","rawId":"Lev.19.28_StudyNote_Filament","t":"link","v":"study note on 19:28"},". Self-mutilation was a pagan custom. Just as defects of any kind precluded most animals as offerings (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.22.19-25","r":"Lev.22.19-25","rawR":"Lev.22.19-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.22.19-25","value":"Lev.22.19-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:19-25"},"), a defect similarly precluded a priest from officiating (see ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.17-23","r":"Lev.21.17-23","rawR":"Lev.21.17-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.17-23","value":"Lev.21.17-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:17-23"},"). For example, a eunuch could not serve as a priest (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.23.1","r":"Deut.23.1","rawR":"Deut.23.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.23.1","value":"Deut.23.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Deut 23:1"},") because he was not an adequate representative of the people. However, his priestly lineage was recognized as qualifying him to eat his priestly share (see ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.22","r":"Lev.21.22","rawR":"Lev.21.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.22","value":"Lev.21.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lev 21:22"},"). On the other hand, uncleanness disqualified any priest from ministry and from eating the priest’s share as long as the condition persisted (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.22.2-8","r":"Lev.22.2-8","rawR":"Lev.22.2-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.22.2-8","value":"Lev.22.2-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:2-8"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Lev.21.5","refs":[{"book":"LEV","endChapter":21,"endVerse":5,"startChapter":21,"startVerse":5}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Lev.21.5","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"LEV","sourceChapterCoverage":[21],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"8792e54d4f3169afbb13ee01d35f425595ce5ac5b924a5d331a2fd750fbc2aba","sourceItemName":"Lev.21.5","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":1499,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"LEV","canonicalOSIS":"Lev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Lev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Lev.21.5","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Lev.21.5","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.6","r":"Lev.21.6","rawR":"Lev.21.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.6","value":"Lev.21.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:6"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," A priest should ",{"c":["never bring shame"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," by profaning God’s name."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Lev.21.6","refs":[{"book":"LEV","endChapter":21,"endVerse":6,"startChapter":21,"startVerse":6}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Lev.21.6","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"LEV","sourceChapterCoverage":[21],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2fb802392b2b18def75052747bc20fab48955b77391aad6e28a5413b5e37e5bb","sourceItemName":"Lev.21.6","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":1500,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"LEV","canonicalOSIS":"Lev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Lev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Lev.21.6","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Lev.21.6","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.7","r":"Lev.21.7","rawR":"Lev.21.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.7","value":"Lev.21.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:7"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The priest, to lead Israel in worship, had to model the highest standard of conduct for the people both in his personal life and in leadership of his family. He could have no ties to pagan culture (prostitution, ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.9","r":"Lev.21.9","rawR":"Lev.21.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.9","value":"Lev.21.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:9"},"), nor could the legitimacy of his family be questioned (divorce). Similar standards applied to leaders of the early church (",{"href":"?bref=1Tim.3.1-13","r":"1Tim.3.1-13","rawR":"1Tim.3.1-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Tim.3.1-13","value":"1Tim.3.1-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Tim 3:1-13"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Lev.21.7","refs":[{"book":"LEV","endChapter":21,"endVerse":7,"startChapter":21,"startVerse":7}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Lev.21.7","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"LEV","sourceChapterCoverage":[21],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"fa9a066164a5dd547fe7972b764bc2730e27c37f67f843c02a4f96424f9c6ddd","sourceItemName":"Lev.21.7","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":1501,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"LEV","canonicalOSIS":"Lev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Lev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Lev.21.7","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Lev.21.7","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.10-15","r":"Lev.21.10-15","rawR":"Lev.21.10-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.10-15","value":"Lev.21.10-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:10-15"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The restrictions made on the common priests (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.1-4","r":"Lev.21.1-4","rawR":"Lev.21.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.1-4","value":"Lev.21.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:1-4"},") applied even more stringently to the ",{"c":["high priest"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," because he had to represent all Israel, including the other priests. • The priest must ",{"c":["never leave his hair uncombed"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," or ",{"c":["tear his clothing"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," in mourning, so that he would always be fit to minister. Although the common priest was permitted to marry a widow, the high priest was allowed to marry only a virgin. This made certain that the future high priest and the common priests descended from that union would have an unquestioned lineage (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.15","r":"Lev.21.15","rawR":"Lev.21.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.15","value":"Lev.21.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Lev.21.10-15","refs":[{"book":"LEV","endChapter":21,"endVerse":15,"startChapter":21,"startVerse":10}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Lev.21.10-15","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"LEV","sourceChapterCoverage":[21],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"93421e40f4a50644da4dc1c037c722f829062d2327a00034ed971a591e5ff1dd","sourceItemName":"Lev.21.10-15","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":1502,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"LEV","canonicalOSIS":"Lev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Lev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Lev.21.10-15","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Lev.21.10-15","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.22","r":"Lev.21.22","rawR":"Lev.21.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.22","value":"Lev.21.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:22"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["he may eat:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," Although a mutilation or defect (see ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.18-20","r":"Lev.21.18-20","rawR":"Lev.21.18-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.18-20","value":"Lev.21.18-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:18-20"},") disqualified a descendant of Aaron from representing the people, it did not compromise his priestly lineage. He was eligible to eat the priest’s share of the offerings (see ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.2.3","r":"Lev.2.3","rawR":"Lev.2.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.2.3","value":"Lev.2.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:3"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.2.10","r":"Lev.2.10","rawR":"Lev.2.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.2.10","value":"Lev.2.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.6.17-18","r":"Lev.6.17-18","rawR":"Lev.6.17-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.6.17-18","value":"Lev.6.17-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:17-18"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Lev.21.22","refs":[{"book":"LEV","endChapter":21,"endVerse":22,"startChapter":21,"startVerse":22}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Lev.21.22","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"LEV","sourceChapterCoverage":[21],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"f15d317b59e1180e4e0a4faf88d77cbfa77b30dd7ca7d245819d9674aaa09d5a","sourceItemName":"Lev.21.22","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":1503,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"LEV","canonicalOSIS":"Lev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Lev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Lev.21.22","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Lev.21.22","type":"StudyNote"}],"version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}